VENDORED: MathLive v0.111.1, full build (web/vendor/mathlive/)

Used only by the browser front end to typeset the LaTeX the `latex` package
emits (issue F_0016) and, since F_0017, to provide the `<math-field>` editor and
the LaTeX-to-AsciiMath conversion the input reader consumes. It is not part of
the published library artifacts, and no Scala code binds to it -- the facades
pass and receive strings.

0.111.1 IS A SECURITY FLOOR, not merely the version that happened to be
current (audits of 2026-10-01 and 2026-10-18). XSS advisories exist against
earlier MathLive releases, all in the convertLatexToMarkup path the page's
MathRender uses: CVE-2025-29049 (\htmlData, <= 0.103.0, fixed 0.104.0),
CVE-2026-54705 (\text{}/\mbox{} unescaped, <= 0.109.2, fixed in exactly
0.110.0), and the five escaping fixes 0.111.1 lists under its Security
Advisories (\enclose attributes, unquoted \htmlData/\href values, MathML
`notation`, SSML text, unvalidated CSS in `style`; re-vendored by F_0145).
A vendored library is invisible to Scala Steward and Dependabot alike, so
nothing automated will ever warn about it: if this file is ever re-vendored,
the replacement must be >= 0.111.1, and the advisory database should be
re-checked the same way. 0.111.0's breaking changes removed only the
MathJSON/compute-engine APIs; convertLatexToMarkup and
convertLatexToAsciiMath were checked present in the new build.

This is the FULL distribution, which replaced the render-only SSR one at F_0017;
it carries the same conversion functions, so one file supersedes the other
rather than joining it. It is UMD, so it loads as a plain `<script src>` and
defines `globalThis.MathLive` before `main.js` runs.

The package's 232 KB of keyboard sounds are NOT vendored, and since this build
does have a virtual keyboard that is now a decision rather than an absence:
`MathfieldElement.soundsDirectory` is set to null in `index.html`. This build
does not bundle any part of `@cortex-js/compute-engine` either: MathLive looks
that up on `globalThis[Symbol.for("io.cortexjs.compute-engine")]` and merely
declines the MathJSON conversions when it is absent -- verified before
vendoring, because shipping a second CAS inside a page whose purpose is the
first one would be absurd.

The 0.111.1 bytes were taken from the npm registry tarball, verified against
the registry's own `dist.integrity` (SHA-512) before extraction. The twenty
KaTeX font files are byte-identical to 0.110.0's, and mathlive-fonts.css
differs only in its version comment. (0.110.0 had come from the jsDelivr
mirror, the registry being unreachable then; the mirror was checked by
re-fetching the previously vendored SSR file against its recorded hash,
DC4B57D226EA371CDBA11727257424879DB7179CCBA851C171AFA782DE90BD10.)

